diagnosis_text:
Affected component: the uplink between the floor’s default gateway and the core is misconfigured. On sshswitch (which holds the 10.5.0.254 gateway), the two uplinks to router17 are bonded in “round-robin” mode and also carry a VLAN 5 subinterface into the bridge.

Mechanism: Per-packet load‑balancing (bonding mode 0) alternates frames across the two physical links. This causes packet reordering and intermittent loss for routed traffic when either link momentarily delays/drops frames. Because all 10.5.0.x users egress via this uplink for off-subnet traffic, they experience simultaneous “freezes.” Local (in subnet) traffic to the gateway remains fine, which matches our tests: PC1/PC2 to 10.5.0.254 showed 0%
